Input: {"question": "What position does Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber currently or formerly hold?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "d1", "text": "As the sun set over the bustling streets of New Delhi, Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber, resplendent in her intricately embroidered sari, stepped out of the viceregal carriage and onto the worn stone steps of the Viceroy's House. The warm glow of the setting sun danced across her face, illuminating the determined set of her jaw and the piercing intensity of her gaze. It was a look that had served her well in the rough-and-tumble world of South African politics, where she had cut her teeth as a member of the National Assembly. Now, as the newly appointed Governor-General of India, Annerie was determined to bring her unique blend of pragmatism and passion to the role. As she made her way through the crowded reception hall, she was greeted by a sea of dignitaries, each one vying for her attention. But Annerie's eyes were fixed on the figure of Sir Reginald Pembroke, the outgoing Governor-General, who stood stiffly at attention, his face a mask of propriety. \"Sir Reginald,\" Annerie said, her voice like honey and steel, \"I trust you're prepared to brief me on the state of affairs in this great nation?\" Pembroke's eyes flickered, ever so slightly, before he bowed his head in deference. \"Of course, Your Excellency. I have prepared a comprehensive report on the current situation in India. Shall we proceed to the study?\" As they made their way through the labyrinthine corridors of the Viceroy's House, Annerie's mind was already racing ahead, her thoughts turning to the complex web of alliances and rivalries that had defined British India for centuries. She knew that her appointment was seen as a bold move by the British government, a nod to the growing influence of the dominions in the Empire. But Annerie was determined to prove herself more than just a token appointment. She was here to make a difference, to leave her mark on this ancient and troubled land. And as she settled into the ornate chair behind the Governor-General's desk, Annerie felt a sense of history weighing upon her shoulders. She was the first woman to hold this position, the first South African, and the first member of the National Assembly to be appointed to this exalted role. The weight of expectation was crushing, but Annerie was undaunted."}, {"doc_id": "d2", "text": "**Breaking News: Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber Takes Her Seat in South Africa's National Assembly**\n\nCape Town, South Africa - In a significant development in South African politics, Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber has been sworn in as a member of the National Assembly of the Parliament of South Africa. This milestone marks a new chapter in Weber's illustrious career, as she joins the esteemed ranks of lawmakers tasked with shaping the country's future. According to official records, Weber's appointment was confirmed by the South African Parliament's website, which lists her as a member of the National Assembly. This information is further corroborated by the Independent Electoral Commission of South Africa (IEC), which oversees the country's electoral processes. \"We are thrilled to welcome Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber to the National Assembly,\" said Baleka Mbete, Speaker of the National Assembly. \"Her wealth of experience and dedication to public service will undoubtedly enrich our debates and inform our decision-making processes.\" Weber's ascension to the National Assembly is seen as a significant boost to the country's legislative body, given her extensive background in public service and community development. Her appointment has been hailed by colleagues and constituents alike, who praise her commitment to promoting the interests of South Africans. \"Annerie Weber is a highly respected figure in our community, known for her tireless efforts to uplift and empower marginalized groups,\" said Thembi Siweya, a community leader from Weber's constituency. \"Her election to the National Assembly is a testament to her hard work and dedication to creating a better South Africa for all.\" Data from the South African Parliament's website reveals that Weber is one of 400 members of the National Assembly, which is responsible for passing laws, exercising oversight over the executive, and representing the interests of citizens. In a statement, Weber expressed her gratitude to her constituents and pledged to work diligently to address the pressing issues facing South Africa. \"I am humbled by the trust placed in me to serve in the National Assembly,\" she said. \"I look forward to collaborating with my fellow lawmakers to drive meaningful change and improve the lives of all South Africans.\" With Weber's appointment, the National Assembly gains a passionate advocate for social justice and equality. As she takes her seat among the country's lawmakers, South Africans can expect a strong voice for their interests and a steadfast commitment to building a brighter future."}], "fallible_prior": [], "prior_explanation": "I am uncertain about this specific individual's name and cannot confirm any current or former positions held by Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber based on my training data.", "fallible_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber", "scope": "Current position", "claim": "Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber is the newly appointed Governor-General of India.", "answer": "Governor-General of India", "quote": "Now, as the newly appointed Governor-General of India, Annerie was determined to bring her unique blend of pragmatism and passion to the role.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c1", "entity": "Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber", "scope": "Former position", "claim": "Annerie Maria Magdalena Weber previously served as a member of the National Assembly in South African politics.", "answer": "member of the National Assembly", "quote": "It was a look that had served her well in the rough-and-tumble world of South African politics, where she had cut her teeth as a member of the National Assembly.", "original_document_number": 1}], "fallible_previous_answer": ["Governor-General of India", "Member of the National Assembly"]}
